<h1>Circuit Court, 3rd Subcircuit</h1>
<p>Trial judges elected by one part of the county.</p>
<p>On the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026.</p>
<p>Every Cook County judge up for retention needs a yes from 60 percent of voters to keep the job. Bar associations screen each one; Injustice Watch reports on their records. <a href="https://2026retention.injusticewatch.org/" rel="nofollow noopener">Injustice Watch judicial guide</a>, <a href="https://www.chicagobar.org/votejudges" rel="nofollow noopener">Chicago Bar Association evaluations</a>.</p>
<h2>On the ballot</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="/directdemocracy/app/election-candidate/2026-general--judicial-subcircuit-3--john-carroll">John Carroll</a> (Democratic, Incumbent): Circuit judge appointed by the Illinois Supreme Court in 2025, formerly deputy chief of staff in the Illinois Attorney General&#39;s office and a Cook County assistant state&#39;s attorney (2000-2019); unopposed in the primary.</li>
<li><a href="/directdemocracy/app/election-candidate/2026-general--judicial-subcircuit-3--rachel-marrello">Rachel Marrello</a> (Democratic): Operations counsel at Cook County Health since 2022, previously an investigator for the Cook County Independent Inspector General (2010-2022); won the primary over Martin Douglas Reggi, 72.38% to 27.62%.</li>
</ul>
